A||||12||My7Fieros||Question for those of you who have installed Mr Mikes seats||||10||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||08-06-2000||01:56 AM||||Well, my Formula is almost finished! And, best part is, Im getting ready to place an order to Mr Mikes for some beachwood leather seats! WOO HOO!!!!!!! <BR>Anyway, my question is, for those of you who have ordered them and installed them yourselves, was it hard? What all did it involve? Ive done all the restoration on my car thusfar on my own (well, me and my roommate) so Im just wondering how hard is it to do, how long did it take you, how did the finished product look, are you happy with it, ect.ect....I cant wait!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||Oreif||08-06-2000||08:19 AM||||The Mr.Mikes Leather Seats are VERY easy. They take about an hour per seat. Mr Mike sends you a video that is VERY detailed in removing your old seat covers and installing the new ones. I had no problems installing mine. Also everything needed to do the job is included! I do mean everything. Razor Blades, Hog rings, 2 hog ring tools, extra padding, extra foam, spray glue,etc. I was very impressed with everything.<BR>My seats came out great. Very high quality. I would highly recommend them to anyone who wanted leather seats!<BR> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Seats.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-06-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||007DOUG||08-06-2000||09:54 AM||||Couldn't agree with you more Oreif.<P>Super quality, super easy,  and EVERYTHING is included.<P>I went for the tan tufted seats. Looks like a Lazy-boy. Love 'em.||||reg||14
Z||000003||rockcrawl||08-06-2000||10:54 AM||||I've used the leather seats from Pisa, and they were also very good quality and easy to install. Hog rings and tool included as well as detailed instructions.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fret Naught||08-06-2000||01:02 PM||||I did my seats last weekend, DITO on what Oreif said, it was piece of cake, MR. Mike is aproaching hero status in my book, I went for the tuft. Style it was a bit more, but I really like it.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SEAT.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FretNaught_sig_4.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||jhogans||08-06-2000||02:02 PM||||DAMN!!!!! Those seats look awesome on both cars.  Now I want a set.||||reg||1
Z||000006||LarryB||08-06-2000||03:57 PM||||Took me more like 4 1/2 hours total, 3 hrs for the first and 1-1/2 for the second, I took my time doing it.  Just have a VCR with remote handy when you do the first seat, you'll probably be rewinding and watching parts again.  Figure on 2-3 weeks to get the seats after you order them, they're worth the wait!<P>The only bad part of the whole thing is that your hands get tired toward the end from doing all the hog ties. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mshill||08-06-2000||06:29 PM||||Fred,  What color is that on your car?  That is what I want to paint my kit project when done.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sluppy123||08-07-2000||06:01 PM||||I agree with everything said above, Mr Mike Is a great guy to deal with and his seats are Top Quality. It took me about 1 1/2 hr. per seat. ||||reg||10
Z||000009||286SE'S||08-07-2000||06:22 PM||||I put my Mr Mikes leather seats in about two and a half years ago. The video is excellent and I watched it twice and did the job with no problems. No one will believe you did it yourself. The are beautiful and comfortable but are not wearing very well. <BR>The piping in the usual wear spot (drivers door side upper bolster has all the leather worn away (about 3"). There are some deep cracks in the seat bottom as well. I have used the recommended polish and they always clean up well except for these two spots. I was expecting longer wear for leather but they actually are not as strong as the cloth seats which lasted  12 years! I can only recommend them for a car that is NOT going to get daily use. By the way Mr Mikes only sells them as a set so I cannot get another to replace my bad one.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000010||My7Fieros||08-08-2000||03:22 AM||||Hmmm, well sounds like a good deal. I cant wait to do it! 286SEs, sorry to hear about the longevity of them though. But, at only 400 bucks for a pair of leather seats, I'll just replace them every couple of years!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (Not that Im made of money or anything, puh-leez, but 400 bucks is cheap for leather seating!)||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||08-08-2000||10:44 AM||||One of the members of our local club has had Mr. Mikes seats for about 3-4 years and his car is a daily driver. He just uses a cheap seat cover over the drivers seat during the weekdays and his bolsters look good. He told me to use mink oil on the seats which keeps them clean and soft. I looked at his seats before I bought mine last year.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Alex4mula||08-08-2000||11:14 AM||||I have had mine for 1.5 years now and still look like new. Install was 2hrs for first and 1 hr for second (learning curve). I think it is the best upgrade in looks for the money on any Fiero.||||reg||1
